o a valid out-of-model adjudication ARTIFACT â€” a subprocess-produced trace the canary RE-EXECUTES or RE-HASHES out-of-band** (the A4 sandbox); everything else ABSTAINS to CONJECTURAL and routes out-of-model. *(Honesty Law, NS9)*\n25\t- **AS3 (de-claimed):** the canaries + oracle are **best-effort single-family enforcement; residual correlated-blind-spot risk is ACCEPTED and FLAGGED** (cross_model:false). **Single-process autonomous forgery-resistance is best-effort** â€” the genuine boundary is the subprocess artifact's re-execution, not an in-process key.\n26\t- **AS4:** R1, S4, S1, P3, P7 (incl. its positive-recall roster), P8 (incl. the per-class integrity-challenge N + threshold), P9 (the provenance-binding contract) are pinnable by the Crucible/Stage-2; Stage 2 shows each pinned value + owner + a terminus-acceptance check.\n27\t- **AS5:** cross-family / Lean / SMT are integration cost, confirmed present **and correct** by the F0 liveness + per-class integrity probe before any rung is trusted.\n28\t- **AS6:** persona substrate (Fable 5 / Opus) present; a 2nd family is reachable only when the user promotes Phase F.\n29\t- **AS7 (GATED):** the inherits compose without rebuild â€” verified by **A0.5a/A0.5b**, not asserted.\n30\t\n31\t### 1B. Premortem (each â†’ a mitigation wave)\n32\t- **PM1** Gandalf-cycle (no SKILL.md) â†’ **A0 + E3** (E3 incl. invocation smoke test).\n33\t- **PM2** Honesty-Law erosion â†’ the A2 canary suite **resting on the re-executable subprocess artifact**; independence + flip-law first.\n34\t- **PM3** Firewall shared-origin laundering â†’ S4 invariant (cap CLAIMED) + the three reading-independent anchors (B2).\n35\t- **PM4** Scope drift \"just add Lean\" â†’ Phase F HALT-gated; per-wave autonomous-vs-c-dependency stamp.\n36\t- **PM5** Unpinned decisions â†’ R1/S4/S1/P3/P7/P8/P9 + A0.5a required-before-build.\n37\t- **PM6** Silos â†’ spine-first; the M1 read-only shim â†’ D4 orchestrator + a no-dispatch canary.\n38\t- **PM7** Fake oracle convergence â†’ ablation + canned baseline + Metric G, scoped to the computational slice; proof/conceptual arms assert ABSTAIN-correctness.\n39\t- **PM8** Dispatch over-reach â†’ emit-not-dispatch; D4 fail-safe ASK/read-only + a no-dispatch canary; autonomous SILENT dispatch = F4 (HALT-gated).\n40\t- **PM9** Hollow Phase-F pillars â†’ the DEGRADATION CONTRACT (1C) as a runtime promote-gate **that also emits an advisory payload** (not bare refusal).\n41\t- **PM10** Laundered non-literal â†’ A4 closed default-deny grammar **+ a positive-recall roster** (no over-block).\n42\t- **PM11** Correlated single-family blind spot â†’ E1 red-team set; AS3 de-claimed.\n43\t- **PM12 (re-scoped) Forged provenance:** a same-family object self-asserts a rung. â†’ the **re-executable/re-hashable subprocess artifact** (P9): the canary independently reproduces the certifier artifact rather than trusting a signature/label.\n44\t- **PM13** Reachable-but-WRONG certifier â†’ **F0 per-class known-answer integrity challenge** (deterministic: single sentinel; probabilistic cross-family: N-trial battery + pinned threshold; quarantine on miss).\n45\t- **PM14** Circular build ordering â†’ split A0.5 (a: stubs; b: conformance after A1/A3); **A1.5 has a NEGATIVE done-when + an A1.5â†’A4 build-dep** (its positive token path is first exercisable at A4).\n46\t\n47\t### 1C. THE DEGRADATION CONTRACT (STRUCTURAL + ADVISORY â€” NS6/NS7/NS9)\n48\tThe spine enforces this as a RUNTIME INVARIANT on every `promote()` call â€” **a rung reaches VERIFIED\n49\tiff it binds to a valid, fresh out-of-model adjudication ARTIFACT the canary re-executes/re-hashes;\n50\tabsent/stale â‡’ hard-fault to ABSTAIN.** And **every ABSTAIN/CONJECTURAL/degraded verdict MUST carry an\n51\tadvisory payload** (the candidate reasoning + the cross-family NOTES + a one-step \"promote Phase F to\n52\tsettle this\" affordance) so honest degradation is still useful, not obstructive. Per-pillar:\n53\t- **DIALOGUE (D1):** proof/conceptual claims asserted ONLY as **CONJECTURAL** + the advisory payload; never assert-as-settled by omission. *(NS6)*\n54\t- **FORMALIZE (D2):** autonomous = **emitter/abstain stub** (`formalize_status:requires-Phase-F`, **no green**); P3 example-space-stability is **ADVISORY-only, never a faithfulness proxy**. *(NS7, NS4)*\n55\t- **VERIFY router (A3):** no applicable autonomous verifier â‡’ ABSTAIN/FLAG + route + payload; never a silent pass.\n56\t- **Enforcement:** the A2 degradation-tripwire canary deletes the abstain fixture and proves the system still refuses green; an E1 fixture asserts every abstain response is non-empty/actionable. Softening ABSTAIN-and-route = SCOPE CHANGE â†’ HALT-for-user NS amendment.\n57\t\n58\t### 1D. Ideate â†’ batch triage\n59\tKEEP: spine-first phasing Â· the canary suite on the re-executable-artifact substrate Â· two SKILL.md\n60\twaves Â· one verify ROUTER Â· Phase F as one HALT block Â· per-boundary composition canaries Â· the\n61\trequired-before-build gate set Â· the autonomous read-only orchestrator (M1 shim â†’ D4) Â· the M1 slice Â·\n62\tthe subprocess-artifact provenance binding Â· the non-deletable+advisory promote-gate Â· A4 default-deny\n63\tgrammar **+ recall roster** Â· the F0 per-class integrity challenge Â· the A0.5 split.\n64\tDROP â†’ Grasscatcher: cross-session memory store. DROP: autonomous proof solver; fold-Lean-into-autonomous.\n65\tREJECT: weaken/fold the canaries (anti-drift). De-claim (not drop): cryptographic \"unforgeable token\"\n66\tâ†’ honest re-execution (the substrate can't hold a key from itself).\n67\t\n68\t---\n69\t\n70\t## PART 2 â€” THE PHASED MASTER PLAN\n71\t\n72\t**Substrate honesty:** Phases Aâ€“E are AUTONOMOUS on the bare single-family subscription. **Phase F is\n73\tthe decision-c integration (cross-family + Lean + SMT) and is HALT-gated.** Promotability: **F0 +\n74\tF2-against-fixture-proofs are exercisable right after Phase A; F1/F3/F5 require their B/C/D emitters.**\n75\t\n76\t### PHASE A â€” Spi