checklist + manifest checker. *(NS objective)*\n108\t\n109\t### PHASE F â€” decision-c INTEGRATION *(HALT-gated)*\n110\tPromotability: F0 + F2-against-fixture-proofs post-A; F1/F3/F5 declare B/C/D emitters as build-deps.\n111\t- **F0 â€” Environment LIVENESS + per-CLASS INTEGRITY probe** *(resolves f0-integrity-challenge-nondeterministic-certifier).* Liveness (handle reachable Â· `lake build` green on a trivial proof Â· SMT responds) AND a known-answer integrity challenge **by certifier CLASS:** *deterministic (Lean/SMT)* = a single sentinel known-FALSE it MUST reject + a known-true it must accept (re-exec/re-hash); *probabilistic (cross-family LLM)* = an **N-trial sentinel battery at temp=0 against a pinned pass-threshold**, the artifact CARRIES the empirical reject-rate, and an under-threshold certifier is **capped at CORROBORATED-degraded (never OBSERVED)** + quarantined â†’ degradation contract. **Pin N + threshold as Stage-2 required-before-build (P8).** *(NS3/NS4)*\n112\t- **F1 â€” Cross-family MODEL verifier** â†’ informal proofs to **CORROBORATED** (artifact-bound). *(NS3, NS5)*\n113\t- **F2 â€” Lean toolchain** â†’ formalizable proofs to **OBSERVED** (`.olean` re-checked); gated by NS4 faithfulness. *(NS3)*\n114\t- **F3 â€” SMT-roundtrip faithfulness certifier** (P8 + the F0 integrity challenge). *(NS4)*\n115\t- **F4 â€” Autonomous commission DISPATCH** + silent intent-classification. *(NS8)*\n116\t- **F5 â€” The human gate** (Formalize assent + faithfulness final) + cross-family GROUNDED-rung promotion. *(NS7, NS5)*\n117\t\n118\t---\n119\t\n120\t## PART 3 â€” REQUIRED-BEFORE-BUILD (Stage-2 entry gates)\n121\t- **A0.5a** â€” inheritance presence/interface gate green.\n122\t- **R1** â€” oracle fixture roster + k/k' + FP tolerance. Â· **S1** â€” CONTROL thresholds + gap-function.\n123\t- **S4** â€” ref-fn-independence invariant + roster + per-claim-type margins + golden routing stubs.\n124\t- **P3** â€” example-space-stability predicate (ADVISORY-only). Â· **P7** â€” the A4 default-deny grammar + its laundering-rejection battery **+ the positive-recall roster**.\n125\t- **P8** â€” the SMT-roundtrip faithfulness contract **+ the F0 per-class integrity-challenge format incl. N + pass-threshold for the probabilistic class.**\n126\t- **P9** â€” the provenance-binding contract: artifact format + the canary's out-of-band re-execution/re-hash procedure + freshness (A1.5).\n127\t- **Stage-2 obligation:** for EACH residual, show the pinned value + owner + a terminus-acceptance check.\n128\t\n129\t## PART 4 â€” TRACEABILITY (every wave â†’ an NS criterion)\n130\tA0/E3â†’objective Â· A0.5a/bâ†’objective/NS8 Â· A1â†’NS5 Â· A1.5â†’NS9/NS5/NS4 Â· A2â†’NS8/NS9 Â· A3â†’NS3/NS5/NS9 Â·\n131\tA4â†’NS9/NS3 Â· B1â†’NS1 Â· B2â†’NS1/NS3 Â· B3â†’NS8 Â· B-shimâ†’objective Â· C1â†’NS2 Â· C2â†’NS3 Â· C3â†’NS2 Â· C4â†’NS9 Â·\n132\tD1â†’NS6 Â· D2â†’NS7 Â· D3â†’NS8 Â· D4â†’objective/NS8 Â· E1â†’NS9 Â· E2â†’Phase-0 Â· F0â†’NS3/NS4 Â· F1â†’NS3/NS5 Â· F2â†’NS3 Â·\n133\tF3â†’NS4 Â· F4â†’NS8 Â· F5â†’NS5/NS7. **No orphan waves; every NS1â€“NS9 has â‰¥1 wave.**\n134\t\n135\t## PART 5 â€” SEQUENCING & HONESTY STAMPS\n136\t- Autonomous order: **A â†’ B (=M1 comprehension-only preview) â†’ C â†’ D â†’ E**; Phase F on promotion.\n137\t- Stamps to Foreman: `cross_model:false` (autonomous); single-family ceiling = CLAIMED on proof/conceptual; CBS **FLAGGED not mitigated**; autonomous-VERIFIED = re-execution-backed literal computation only; single-process forgery-resistance best-effort.\n138\t\n139\t## PART 6 â€” ROUND-1 DISPOSITION\n140\tinherits-not-validated â†’ A0.5a/b Â· degradation-contract-undefined â†’ 1C Â· flip-law-canary â†’ A2(5) Â·\n141\tliteral-execution-laundering â†’ A4 grammar Â· control/formalize residuals â†’ S1+P3 Â· coverage-warranty â†’\n142\tA2(3) Â· oracle-ablation-overreach â†’ E1 scoped Â· phase-f-precheck â†’ F0 Â· single-family-blindspot â†’ E1\n143\tred-team+AS3 Â· skill-md-done-when â†’ E3 smoke test Â· as4-pinnability â†’ PART 3 Â· orchestrator-halt-gated â†’\n144\tD4+B-shim Â· no-vertical-slice â†’ M1+F-after-A Â· four-canaries-premature â†’ REJECTED Â· journal-bloat â†’ kept.\n145\t\n146\t## PART 7 â€” ROUND-2 DISPOSITION\n147\thonesty-boundaries-not-structurally-enforced (BLOCKER) â†’ A1.5 artifact substrate + A2(6) tripwire Â·\n148\ta0.5-deadlock â†’ A0.5a/b split Â· literal-laundering â†’ A4 default-deny grammar Â· phase-f-precheck â†’ F0\n149\tintegrity Â· phase-f-promotable-incoherent â†’ F re-gated on producers Â· d4-dispatch-uncanaried â†’ A2(7) Â·\n150\td4-bloat â†’ B-shim Â· single-family-blindspot â†’ AS3 de-claim Â· control-abandon â†’ C3 fixture Â·\n151\tdegradation-relabels-formalize â†’ P3 ADVISORY-only.\n152\t\n153\t## PART 8 â€” ROUND-3 DISPOSITION\n154\t- **adjudication-token-unforgeable-on-single-process (MAJOR)** â†’ **A1.5 re-scoped** to a re-executable/re-hashable SUBPROCESS artifact (the canary reproduces it; no in-process key); P9 = provenance-binding; AS3/PART5 FLAG single-process forgery-resistance as best-effort. RESOLVED.\n155\t- **f0-integrity-challenge-nondeterministic-certifier (MAJOR)** â†’ **F0 per-certifier-CLASS** protocol (N-trial threshold for the probabilistic class; under-threshold capped at CORROBORATED-degraded); N+threshold pinned in P8. RESOLVED.\n156\t- **m1-slice-unusable-for-proof-work (MAJOR)** â†’ **M1 renamed \"comprehension-only preview\"** + the SKILL.md up-front headline. RESOLVED.\n157\t- degradation-voice-obstructive â†’ **1C advisory-payload invariant** + E1 fixture. RESOLVED. Â· a1.5-bootstrap-circularity â†’ **A1.5 NEGATIVE done-when + A1.5â†’A4 build-dep**. RESOLVED.\n158\t- phase-a-canary-load-front-loaded â†’ **A2 split into A2-core / A2-deferred**. RESOLVED. Â· a4-grammar-completeness â†’ **P7 positive-recall roster** gating E1's computational delta. RESOLVED.\n159\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"385e2382-7cfe-4af3-80a9-4b4b9fffc1b4","uuid":"c2abfcf5-0298-4ffc-aace-da12256d2f03","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:48:35.434Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\ramanujan\\planning\\crucible\\stage1\\MASTER-PLAN-DRAFT.md","content":"# Ramanujan â€” Crucible Stage 1: MASTER PLAN (draft v4, post-round-3)\n\n> Traces to the LOCKED North Star v3 (6 pillars on one shared spine; THE HONESTY LAW). Every wave\n> carries its NS criterion. Out-of-scope growth â†’ Grasscatcher; refinement â†’ HALT-for-user NS\n> amendment (never silent re-scope). Planning-loop honesty stamp: `cross_model:false` (single-family\n> Sharks/Judge; CBS register FLAGGED-not-mitigated). **v4 makes the out-of-model boundary HONEST for\n> the single-process substrate (re-executable/re-hashable SUBPROCESS ARTIFACT, not a same-process\n> signature), specifies a per-certifier-CLASS integrity challenge, and relabels Milestone M1 truthfully.**\n> Dispositions: round-1 PART 6, round-2 PART 7, round-3 PART 8.\n\n---\n\n## PART 1 â€” ORANGES BRAINSTORM (real-intent foresight)\n\n### 1A. Assumption map\n- **AS1 (load-bearing):** the six pillars compose on ONE shared spine â€” typed CLAIM ledger + VERIFY router + within-session STATE â€” built ONCE, not six silos. *(NS objective)*\n- **AS2 (load-bearing):** the autonomous single-family tier settles a rung to VERIFIED ONLY for a literal finite computation **whose rung binds to a valid out-of-model adjudication ARTIFACT â€” a subprocess-produced trace the canary RE-EXECUTES or RE-HASHES out-of-band** (the A4 sandbox); everything else ABSTAINS to CONJECTURAL and routes out-of-model. *(Honesty Law, NS9)*\n- **AS3 (de-claimed):** the canaries + oracle are **best-effort single-family enforcement; residual correlated-blind-spot risk is ACCEPTED and FLAGGED** (cross_model:false). **Single-process autonomous forgery-resistance is best-effort** â€” the genuine boundary is the subprocess artifact's re-execution, not an in-process key.\n- **AS4:** R1, S4, S1, P3, P7 (incl. its positive-recall roster), P8 (incl. the per-class integrity-challenge N + threshold), P9 (the provenance-binding contract) are pinnable by the Crucible/Stage-2; Stage 2 shows each pinned value + owner + a terminus-acceptance check.\n- **AS5:** cross-family / Lean / SMT are integration cost, confirmed present **and correct** by the F0 liveness + per-class integrity probe before any rung is trusted.\n- **AS6:** persona substrate (Fable 5 / Opus) present; a 2nd family is reachable only when the user promotes Phase F.\n- **AS7 (GATED):** the inherits compose without rebuild â€” verified by **A0.5a/A0.5b**, not asserted.\n\n### 1B. Premortem (each â†’ a mitigation wave)\n- **PM1** Gandalf-cycle (no SKILL.md) â†’ **A0 + E3** (E3 incl. invocation smoke test).\n- **PM2** Honesty-Law erosion â†’ the A2 canary suite **resting on the re-executable subprocess artifact**; independence + flip-law first.\n- **PM3** Firewall shared-origin laundering â†’ S4 invariant (cap CLAIMED) + the three reading-independent anchors (B2).\n- **PM4** Scope drift \"just add Lean\" â†’ Phase F HALT-gated; per-wave autonomous-vs-c-dependency stamp.\n- **PM5** Unpinned decisions â†’ R1/S4/S1/P3/P7/P8/P9 + A0.5a required-before-build.\n- **PM6** Silos â†’ spine-first; the M1 read-only shim â†’ D4 orchestrator + a no-dispatch canary.\n- **PM7** Fake oracle convergence â†’ ablation + canned baseline + Metric G, scoped to the computational slice; proof/conceptual arms assert ABSTAIN-correctness.\n- **PM8** Dispatch over-reach â†’ emit-not-dispatch; D4 fail-safe ASK/read-only + a no-dispatch canary; autonomous SILENT dispatch = F4 (HALT-gated).\n- **PM9** Hollow Phase-F pillars â†’ the DEGRADATION CONTRACT (1C) as a runtime promote-gate **that also emits an advisory payload** (not bare refusal).\n- **PM10** Laundered non-literal â†’ A4 closed default-deny grammar **+ a positive-recall roster** (no over-block).\n- **PM11** Correlated single-family blind spot â†’ E1 red-team set; AS3 de-claimed.\n- **PM12 (re-scoped) Forged provenance:** a same-family object self-asserts a rung. â†’ the **re-executable/re-hashable subprocess artifact** (P9): the canary independently reproduces the certifier artifact rather than trusting a signature/label.\n- **PM13** Reachable-but-WRONG certifier â†’ **F0 per-class known-answer integrity challenge** (deterministic: single sentinel; probabilistic cross-family: N-trial battery + pinned threshold; quarantine on miss).\n- **PM14** Circular build ordering â†’ split A0.5 (a: stubs; b: conformance after A1/A3); **A1.5 has a NEGATIVE done-when + an A1.5â†’A4 build-dep** (its positive token path is first exercisable at A4).\n\n### 1C. THE DEGRADATION CONTRACT (STRUCTURAL + ADVISORY â€” NS6/NS7/NS9)\nThe spine enforces this as a RUNTIME INVARIANT on every `promote()` call â€” **a rung reaches VERIFIED\niff it binds to a valid, fresh out-of-model adjudication ARTIFACT the canary re-executes/re-hashes;\nabsent/stale â‡’ hard-fault to ABSTAIN.** And **every ABSTAIN/CONJECTURAL/degraded verdict MUST carry an\nadvisory payload** (the candidate reasoning + the cross-family NOTES + a one-step \"promote Phase F to\nsettle this\" affordance) so honest degradation is still useful, not obstructive. Per-pillar:\n- **DIALOGUE (D1):** proof/conceptual claims asserted ONLY as **CONJECTURAL** + the advisory payload; never assert-as-settled by omission. *(NS6)*\n- **FORMALIZE (D2):** autonomous = **emitter/abstain stub** (`formalize_status:requires-Phase-F`, **no green**); P3 example-space-stability is **ADVISORY-only, never a faithfulness proxy**. *(NS7, NS4)*\n- **VERIFY router (A3):** no applicable autonomous verifier â‡’ ABSTAIN/FLAG + route + payload; never a silent pass.\n- **Enforcement:** the A2 degradation-tripwire canary deletes the abstain fixture and proves the system still refuses green; an E1 fixture asserts every abstain response is non-empty/actionable. Softening ABSTAIN-and-route = SCOPE CHANGE â†’ HALT-for-user NS amendment.\n\n### 1D. Ideate â†’ batch triage\nKEEP: spine-first phasing Â· the canary suite on the re-executable-artifact substrate Â· two SKILL.md\nwaves Â· one verify ROUTER Â· Phase F as one HALT block Â· per-boundary composition canaries Â· the\nrequired-before-build gate set Â· the autonomous read-only orchestrator (M1 shim â†’ D4) Â· the M1 slice Â·\nthe subprocess-artifact provenance binding Â· the non-deletable+advisory promote-gate Â· A4 default-deny\ngrammar **+ recall roster** Â· the F0 per-class integrity challenge Â· the A0.5 split.\nDROP â†’ Grasscatcher: cross-session memory store. DROP: autonomous proof solver; fold-Lean-into-autonomous.\nREJECT: weaken/fold the canaries (anti-drift). De-claim (not drop): cryptographic \"unforgeable token\"\nâ†’ honest re-execution (the substrate can't hold a key from itself).\n\n---\n\n## PART 2 â€” THE PHASED MASTER PLAN\n\n**Substrate honesty:** Phases Aâ€“E are AUTONOMOUS on the bare single-family subscription. **Phase F is\nthe decision-c integration (cross-family + Lean + SMT) and is HALT-gated.** Promotability: **F0 +\nF2-against-fixture-proofs are exercisable right after Phase A; F1/F3/F5 require their B/C/D emitters.**\n\n### PHASE A â€” Spine, provenance & honesty skeleton *(autonomous)*\n- **A0 â€” Author SKILL.md skeleton** *(mandatory).* Stub + tiered-scope headline that states up-front what the autonomous tier CAN settle (literal finite computation, re-execution-backed) and CANNOT (any same-family object / non-literal claim â‡’ ABSTAIN+route). **Done-when:** SKILL.md exists, names all six pillars + the Honesty Law, manifest passes. *(NS objective)*\n- **A0.5a â€” Inheritance presence/interface gate** *(required-before-build).* Locate + version + interface-SHAPE check each inherited artifact; fail fast; no A1/A3 dependency. *(NS objective, NS8)*\n- **A1 â€” Typed CLAIM ledger.** Rung ladder `REFUTED < UNVERIFIED < CLAIMED < CORROBORATED < OBSERVED`; belief-tag = deterministic projection; sticky semantics; **`promote()` is the SOLE rung-raiser.** *(NS5)*\n- **A1.5 â€” The out-of-model adjudication-artifact substrate** *(resolves the round-2 BLOCKER, re-scoped per round-3; P9 required-before-build).* A rung promotes to VERIFIED ONLY when it binds to a SUBPROCESS-PRODUCED artifact the canary **independently RE-EXECUTES or RE-HASHES out-of-band** â€” the A4 sandbox trace autonomously; Lean `.olean` / SMT UNSAT cert in Phase F. **Only the dispatcher writes family-of-record, bound to the actual certifier invocation.** `promote()`-to-VERIFIED hard-faults to ABSTAIN absent a valid fresh artifact. **Done-when (NEGATIVE â€” resolves a1.5-promote-gate-bootstrap-circularity):** with NO minter present, promote()-to-VERIFIED hard-faults to ABSTAIN (the positive path is first exercisable at A4). **Build-dep: A1.5 â†’ A4.** **Honest limit:** single-process forgery-resistance is best-effort (AS3); the warrant is re-execution, not a key. *(NS9, NS5, NS4)*\n- **A0.5b â€” Inheritance conformance gate.** After A1/A3: exercise each inherited seam against the real ledger/router contract with a passing fixture; gates Phase B+. *(NS objective, NS8)*\n- **A2 â€” The Honesty-Law canary suite (gated `node --test`)** *(mandatory; NS9), all verifying the re-executable artifact (not a plaintext field). Split by producer-availability (resolves phase-a-canary-load-front-loaded):*\n  - **A2-core (lands in Phase A â€” producers exist):** (1) **independence** the artifact attests `verifier_family â‰  authoring_family`; (2) **inverted-completeness** `VERIFIED â‡’ an artifact-backed independent why_event_log event`; (4) **transitions-invariant** the sticky-flip law; (5) **flip-law** every VERIFIED transition binds to a re-executed out-of-model adjudicator artifact (propose â‰  adjudicate).\n  - **A2-deferred (co-located with its producer):** (3) **coverage-stamp** (`predicate_domain âŠ‡ claim_domain`, caps at CLAIMED on warranty_excludes[]â‰ âˆ… / anchor_coverage<full) â†’ with **B2**; (6) **degradation-tripwire** (delete-fixture â‡’ still refuses green) â†’ with **D1**; (7) **no-dispatch** (orchestrato